From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:14:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 6th grade: the Ice Rink (unit 5, negative numbers)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thermometer (what negatives mean in stories, negatives on the number
line, opposites), Rink Lines (negative decimals and fractions on the
number line), Race Board (comparing on a number line and without one,
ordering, writing inequalities from temperatures), and Ice Depth
(absolute value, comparing and ordering absolute values, absolute value
in words). 12 Khan skills and 4 new mix-ups, including "a negative with
bigger digits is bigger". Answer boxes can now take negative numbers:
a ± button sits beside the box (phone keypads have no minus key), and
a typed - or − is kept. Opens after the Clock Tower Unit Test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014wQFE2KZBjkYxaH2m8t9SR
